/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/docs/paper/sections/abstract.tex:5:Yet instance-level selection yields ${<}1$\,pp on most datasets; a four-stage diagnostic cascade localizes this \textbf{correlation-selection gap}: the optimal strategy is dataset-dependent (LP-best: $+8$\,pp on Few-NERD; MV dominates on CoNLL) and near-zero selection alignment ($\alpha{\to}0$), not degeneracy alone, is the binding constraint.
